 bool CanSetAsDefaultBrowser() {
-  return GetDefaultBrowserSetPermission() != SET_DEFAULT_NOT_ALLOWED;
+  // Hook Browser: not yet, and the browser should not pretend otherwise.
+  //
+  // Everything that asks the user to "make this your default browser" -- the
+  // startup prompt, the settings toggle, the onboarding step -- is gated on this
+  // answer. It is false because nothing registers this binary as a browser on
+  // Windows: no ProgID under `HKCU\Software\Classes`, no entry under
+  // `Software\Clients\StartMenuInternet`. The prompt's second step is "click Set
+  // default in your Windows settings", and Hook Browser is not in that list, so
+  // the user is talked through a flow that cannot complete. A browser that asks
+  // for something it cannot be given teaches people to ignore it.
+  //
+  // The default-browser work inverts this: registration (ProgIDs, the client key,
+  // an MSIX `windows.protocol` extension) plus a deep link to our own settings
+  // page, and then this returns the real answer again. Until then, false is the
+  // truth -- `docs/browser-poc-plan.md`, "Default-browser registration".
+  return false;
 }
 
